  "_comment": [
    "Up where nothing walks, `low`'s antonym. `high clouds` lifts the cloud deck far above, `high landmass` towers,",
    "`high sea` stands the water as high as `deep` does, and `high structures` are built raised over the ground.",
    "`high gravity` pulls harder, `high grass` grows tall, and `high obelisks` (spikes, pyramids, arches, pedestals,",
    "piles) stand twice as tall; `high lakes` lie up on the high ground, a `high aurora` hangs overhead, and a high",
    "sun or moon climbs overhead on its way across. A high Age towers under far clouds, and now and then has a high",
    "sea, raised structures, tall grass, tall formations or high lakes too; never a heavier pull, which only an",
    "aimed word turns."
